Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-15-2001||11:52 AM||||yesterday i got the exhaust manifolds hooked up and i put the lead pipe on so i decided to see if it would fire off. i tried for about 2 minutes and it didn't start so my dad decided to spray starting fluid in the intake. as i turns out the distributor was off so the plug wires were in the wrong place so when i tried to start it again with the either it back fired and caught on fire. i blew it out pretty quick so nothing got damaged. after i got the firing order right i hit the key and she popped right off.<BR>i just loved the sound of that 2.8 with the strait pipe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> . <P>now all i have to do is wait for my ALT. bracket to come in the mail from kick hill and tomorrow the parking brake cables and battery box should be coming from the fiero store. then i have to spend $200 on a windshield. after all of that is done i will be done with it for this year. i hope  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .<P>i will have about $700 in my 85 GT total not including the paint job i will do in the spring.<P>i just don't like the fact that my FIERO cought FIRE before it even started running  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||1
